    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "Write the relationship check-in email body now.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "={{ $('Prepare').item.json.tone + '\\n\\n--- Client ---\\nName: ' + $('Prepare').item.json.name + '\\nOur history / notes: ' + ($('Prepare').item.json.note || '(none provided)') + '\\n\\nThis is check-in number ' + $('Prepare').item.json.checkInNumber + '. Your PREVIOUS check-in to this client was:\\n' + ($('Prepare').item.json.lastMessage || '(none yet — this is the first one)') + '\\n\\nWrite a clearly DIFFERENT message from the previous one: a different opening line, a different angle, and different wording. Vary the focus each time (e.g. a simple hello, asking about their team, a seasonal note, curiosity about their plans, a memory from the project). Do not reuse the same sentences or structure.\\n\\nWrite ONLY the email body (no subject line, no placeholders). Warm, personal, 3-5 sentences. Ask how they and their business are doing and reference our past work together when it fits naturally. This is a relationship check-in, NOT a sales pitch — do not promote services, pricing, or ask for new business. Do NOT add any sign-off, closing line, signature, or name (such as Warm regards or [Your Name]) — a signature is appended automatically, so end with your final sentence.' }}"
        }
